In article <6772@medusa.cs.purdue.edu> bee@cs.purdue.edu (Zaphod Beeblebrox) 
writes:

% Indeed.  A scroll of genocide and 3 or 4 food rations is almost a
% guaranteed win in 2.3.  I'm presuming that in 3.0, a scroll of
% genocide will only destroy a particular type of monster, not all of
% those represented by a particular letter, right?

Yes.  The problem, of course is that all dragons are represented by a `D' 
in NetHack irrespective of their colour.  Ergo, they all get wiped out with 
the genociding of that particular alphabet.  More of an implementation 
problem than a conceptual one, methinks.

A fix to this would to be use `inverse-video'-ed alphabets for monsters as
well.  Thus a red dragon could be an IV-ed R, and so on.  During the 
genocide (which I think should be completely eliminated as a possibility
in the game) you could prefix the alphabet with some other non-alphabetic
character like a \ or something to get to the IV-ed monster alphabet.
The IV process would effectively double the maximum number of monsters that
you can have.  Like the rodents-of-unusual-size, Tritons, and all the other
delightful creatures of Omega.

Then again, as I said before, just no to Nethack and play Omega instead. 
Where men are men and getting scared to death is only too common!

Enjoy.

